+
+## PostgreSQL Issue Copy and Deep Subtree Duplication Procedure
+
+Cloning work items, hierarchical sub-tasks, and attachments is governed by an atomic, security-definer PostgreSQL and service layer workflow (`kanban/services/issue_copy.py` and `p3_08_issue_copy.up.sql`):
+
+1. **Authorization Gate:**
+   - Requires `Capability.VIEW` (0x01) on the source issue and `Capability.EDIT` (0x04) on the target project. Missing permissions fail closed with 404 or 403.
+2. **Subtree Traversal and Fail-Closed Pruning:**
+   - Invokes `issues_get_copy_subtrees(p_root_id uuid)` (`SECURITY DEFINER`, `ltree` depth `<= 6`).
+   - Evaluates caller capability on each descendant node (`app_has_object_capability(r.id, 1)`).
+   - If an intermediate or leaf sub-issue lacks `VIEW` permission, the function prunes that node and its descendants fail-closed, aggregating pruned counts into `skipped.restricted_sub_issues` without leaking unauthorized metadata.
+3. **Safety Caps:**
+   - Enforces `MAX_READABLE_ISSUES_LIMIT = 200` to prevent unbounded memory allocation and database timeouts during tree replication.
+4. **Agent-Safe Sequence Allocation:**
+   - Calls `allocate_issue_sequences(p_project_id, p_count, false)` (`p4_24_agent_safe_sequences.up.sql`) to allocate contiguous sequence numbers atomically.
+   - Any skipped sequences are recorded with an immutable `SEQUENCE_SKIPPED` ledger event.
+5. **Atomic Savepoint Registration:**
+   - Executes inside an atomic nested transaction (`session.begin_nested()`).
+   - Cloned issues and sub-issues invoke `register_object(CAST('issue' AS object_kind), ...)` to bind spine records.
+   - Copies attachments when requested (`include_attachments=true`), links relates-to edges (`link_as_relates_to=true`), and emits `ISSUE_CREATED` and `ISSUE_COPIED` activity records.
